// @@@ The state of the bit set is inverted for every bit index from 'fromIndex' to 'toIndex' (both inclusive). The condition 'fromIndex>=0 && toIndex>=fromIndex' ensures that the range of indices is valid. The assertion implies that for all 'i' in the range from 'fromIndex' to 'toIndex' (both inclusive), the bit at index 'i' is inverted from its previous state.

